 ### Optimized runtime and fixture qualification
 
 The Android runtime copy uses a fresh two-day test certificate generated with JDK 21 `keytool`; no publisher signing variable is accepted. The source and destination must be different resolved files/inodes. Verify that the input is unsigned, align a temporary copy, sign that copy with `--debuggable-apk-permitted false`, verify its signature/alignment, and record the unchanged original SHA-256. The keystore lives in runner temporary storage and is deleted; artifact globs include APKs and public verification records, never the key. Different debug/test certificates require an explicit uninstall between variants. Independent release review executed the helper against the real optimized APK and checked signature/alignment, original ZIP entry bytes, production-variable rejection, and exact/symlink/hard-link input/output rejection.
